<Pathway xmlns="http://pathvisio.org/GPML/2021" title="selinene biosynthesis" organism="cellular organisms" source="PlantCyc" version="20260304101735">
  <Description>&lt;i&gt;Supporting evidence for this pathway in Oryza sativa Japonica Group&lt;/i&gt;: Enzyme(s) that catalyzes one or more of the key reactions in this pathway were predicted in Oryza sativa Japonica Group. &lt;A href=&quot;http://www.plantcyc.org/about/savi_pipeline&quot;&gt;[more info]&lt;/A&gt; &lt;i&gt;Summary from MetaCyc:&lt;/i&gt; Selinene is a cyclic sesquiterpene and several stereo isomeric forms are availble in plants. It forms a major component in celery oil. |FRAME: CPD-21652|, |FRAME: CPD-11504|, 7-epi-, 6-epi selinene are some of the forms that have been isolated and synthesized. The autooxidation of |FRAME: CPD-11504| is known to posses antimalarial properties |CITS: [Berlingheri92]|. The biotransformation of this compound has been studied with the use of a plant fungus Glomerula cingulate |CITS: [MIYAZAWA97]|.</Description>
